            <h2>The Problem with Meetings</h2>
            <p>Here's the math. You have 8 people in a room for 60 minutes. That's 8 hours of human time. If that meeting runs 20 minutes over because nobody was tracking the agenda, you just burned almost 3 hours of collective productivity on topics that could have been parked for later.</p>
            <p>The fix isn't fewer meetings. It's <em>structured</em> meetings. Every single person in a meeting should either be receiving value or providing value. If they're doing neither, something is broken.</p>

            <h2>What AgendaClock Does</h2>
            <p>AgendaClock is a visual meeting timeline with countdown timers for each agenda item. You build your agenda, assign time to each topic, and the tool renders a real-time graphical display that everyone in the meeting can see.</p>

