            <h2>Why Visual Timers Work</h2>
            <p>People talk more than others. That's not a personality flaw, it's a facilitation problem. When there's no visible constraint, some voices fill the void while others go quiet. A visible timer externalizes the constraint. It's not <em>you</em> cutting someone off - it's the clock.</p>
            <p>Use <a href="http://www.agile-ux.com/2010/12/16/parking-lot-a-good-facilitation-tool/" target="_blank" style="color: #1a73e8;">parking lots</a> and action items to follow up on discussions that need more air. Allocate times to sprint demos and standup until you no longer need to strictly measure time.</p>

